diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index be767a0..cdaa2af 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 - Store item costs in the data file as whole cents (`cost_cents`), data file version 2. Version 1 files are upgraded when read.
 - Fix: a transfer from a location to itself added stock there. It is now refused.
 - `Inventory.on_hand()` now returns the quantity at each location; the new `Inventory.total()` returns the sum.
+- `Inventory.receive()`, `issue()`, `transfer()` and `adjust()` return the `seq` of the movement they record.
 
 ## 1.4.0
 
diff --git a/docs/reference.md b/docs/reference.md
index e9c3e92..feef123 100644
--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -51,10 +51,10 @@ One JSON document. Item SKUs and location codes are stored upper-case.
 | `Inventory.on_hand(sku)` | `quantity by location` | dict of location code to quantity, leaving out locations holding none |
 | `Inventory.total(sku)` | `total quantity` | sum over every location; 0 when none is held |
 | `Inventory.at(sku, location)` | `quantity at location` | 0 when none is held there |
-| `Inventory.receive(sku, qty, location)` | `quantity at location` | after the goods arrive |
-| `Inventory.issue(sku, qty, location)` | `quantity at location` | what is left there |
-| `Inventory.transfer(sku, qty, source, dest)` | `quantity at destination` | after the goods arrive |
-| `Inventory.adjust(sku, location, counted)` | `change applied` | counted minus what was recorded |
+| `Inventory.receive(sku, qty, location)` | `movement seq` | `seq` of the movement recorded |
+| `Inventory.issue(sku, qty, location)` | `movement seq` | `seq` of the movement recorded |
+| `Inventory.transfer(sku, qty, source, dest)` | `movement seq` | `seq` of the movement recorded |
+| `Inventory.adjust(sku, location, counted)` | `movement seq` | `seq` of the movement recorded |
 
